      "county_name": "Lapin hyvinvointialue",
      "text": "Lapland has no radiotherapy unit, so patients go to OYS in Oulu, and 20 of 21 municipalities are beyond the 100 km commuting threshold [S52, S60].\n\n1. The head of radiotherapy at OYS could evaluate a single 8 Gy session as the default for uncomplicated painful bone metastases, giving equal pain relief with more retreatment [S31, S30, S62]. Within 30 days, the clinical team reviews its default, serving \"Patients receive treatment within target times\" [S25, S24].\n\n2. The OYS breast lead could evaluate 5 sessions as the default for eligible patients (whole breast or chest wall without nodal radiotherapy), naming distance as a reason, as it is non-inferior to 15 sessions [S9, S11, S15]. Within 30 days, the clinical team reviews its eligibility criteria, serving \"National targets and key effectiveness indicators defined for agreed cancers\" [S15, S14, S61].\n\n3. The director of cancer services could propose publishing schedule mix and radiotherapy use by distance band every year, since living far away goes with lower palliative radiotherapy use [S27, S21]. Within 30 days, the director of cancer services and the clinical team decide which data to request from OYS, serving \"Regional differences in treatment are available and used to steer services (cross-cutting indicator)\" [S26].\n\nDistances are modelled road routes from municipality centre points and the current schedule mix is unknown, so effects are estimates [S59, S60, S57].",
